# Web Search with Exa

Use Exa AI for general web searches. For code/library documentation, use 
the find-docs skill instead.

## API Configuration

Set your Exa API key:

```bash
export EXA_API_KEY=your_key
```

Or it can be provided in your agent settings.

## Usage

```bash
# Quick balanced search (default)
web-search "query search terms" [numResults]

# Fast search (lower latency)
web-search "query" --fast

# Deep research (more thorough)
web-search "query" --deep
```

## When to Use This Skill

| Use web-search | Use find-docs (ctx7) |
|---------------|-------------------|
| General questions | Library/framework docs |
| Articles, tutorials | API reference |
| News, trends | Code examples |
| "How do I use X" for general topics | "How do I use X" for a specific library |
| Technology comparisons | Framework-specific questions |

## General Examples

```bash
# Find tutorials on a topic
web-search "best practices for React state management 2024"

# Search for articles
web-search "web assembly trends 2024"

# Technology comparison
web-search "Next.js vs Remix vs Astro comparison"
```

## Notes

- This skill is for general web discovery
- For specific library/framework docs, use find-docs (ctx7)
- exa works without specifying --auto type (balanced by default)